[require map::track::entry [opt [vset VERSION]]]
[description]

This package provides a [package map::display] attachment extending the map's behaviour.
This attachment enables the user to enter an open series of points, i.e. a [term geo/track].
Optionally the series can be closed, i.e. a loop, as needed for a [term geo/area].

[para] While editing is enabled the user edits the track with the mouse:

[list_begin itemized]
[item] Clicking mouse button 1 on a segment of the track inserts a new point into that segment.
[item] Clicking mouse button 1 elsewhere on the map adds a new point, attached to the nearer end of
the track. For a closed track the first three points are added this way. After that new points
can be added only on segments.
[item] Dragging a point with mouse button 2 moves it.
[item] Clicking mouse button 1 on a point removes it.
[list_end]

[para] Panning and zooming the map work as usual. On zoom changes the track is redrawn at its
geographical location.

[para] The attachment knows the zoom level and the viewport of the map only from the view changes
the map reports through its option [option -on-view-change]. Therefore create the attachment
before the map reports its view for the first time, i.e. right after creating the map, or move or
zoom the map (e.g. with its method [method center]) afterwards. Until the attachment knows the zoom
level of the map, no track can be entered or set.

[section API]

[list_begin definitions]
[call [cmd ::map::track::entry] [arg objectName] [arg map] [opt [arg options]...]]

Creates a new track entry attachment [arg objectName] for the [package map::display] widget
[arg map], configured with the specified options. The result of the command is the fully
qualified name of the new object. The command is also available as [cmd {map track entry}].

[para] The attachment takes over the option [option -on-view-change] of [arg map]. The previous
value of that option is remembered and still invoked for each view change. Do not change that
option of the map after creating the attachment.

[para] Editing is initially enabled.

[para] The attachment supports the following options. All of them can be set only at creation
time.

[list_begin options]
[opt_def -closed [arg boolean]]

If true, the edited series of points is closed, i.e. a loop. A loop requires at least three
points. The default is [const false], i.e. an open track.

[opt_def -on-track-change [arg cmdprefix]]

A command prefix which is invoked when the track was changed, with one additional argument, the
new track. The track is a list of geo locations, i.e. latitude/longitude pairs, the points of the
track in order, as in the [const geo] element of a [term geo/track] value described in
[package map::track::file]. The result of the command is ignored.

[para] The command is invoked for changes made by the user, and by method [method clear], but not
by method [method set].

[para] The default is the empty string, i.e. changes are not reported.

[opt_def -on-active [arg cmdprefix]]

A command prefix which is invoked when the mouse pointer enters or leaves a point or the line of
the track. It is invoked with two additional arguments, a handle of the internal editor, to be
ignored, and an identifier of the entered element: the index of the point, counting from 0, the
string [const line] for the line, or the empty string when the last entered element was left.
The result of the command is ignored.

[para] The default is the empty string, i.e. nothing is reported.

[list_end]
[list_end]

The attachment supports the standard methods [method cget] and [method configure], and the
following methods:

[list_begin definitions]
[call [arg objectName] [method enable]]

Enables editing of the track by the user. The result of the method is the empty string.

[call [arg objectName] [method disable]]

Disables editing of the track by the user. The track stays visible. The result of the method is
the empty string.

[call [arg objectName] [method active]]

Returns a boolean value, [const true] if editing is enabled, and [const false] otherwise.

[call [arg objectName] [method track]]

Returns the current track, in the format described for option [option -on-track-change].

[call [arg objectName] [method set] [arg geos]]

Shows the track [arg geos], in the format described for option [option -on-track-change],
replacing the current track, and then centers and zooms the map to fit the track, as method
[method fit] does.

[para] The result of the method is the empty string.

[call [arg objectName] [method clear]]

Removes the current track. The result of the method is the empty string.

[call [arg objectName] [method fit]]

Centers the map on the current track, at the highest zoom level at which the whole track is
visible. Does nothing if the track has less than two points.

[para] The result of the method is the empty string.

[call [arg objectName] [method focus] [arg index]]

Centers the map on the point of the track with the specified [arg index], counting from 0, at the
highest zoom level at which this point and its neighbours in the track are visible.

[para] The result of the method is the empty string.

[list_end]

[section EXAMPLE]

[example {
package require map::provider::osm
package require map::display
package require map::track::entry

map provider osm tiles [file join $env(HOME) .cache osm-tiles]
map display .map -provider tiles -initial-geo {48.05 11.1} -initial-zoom 10
pack .map -fill both -expand 1

map track entry trackentry .map -on-track-change {apply {{geos} {
    puts "track: $geos"
}}}
}]

